{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1520085-what-gifts-can-each-type-of-character-buy","id":1520085,"title":"What gifts can each type of character buy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-08T01:09:30-07:00","id":1520085,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What gifts can each type of character buy?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I am unclear what types of gifts the characters can purchase with XP after character creation. Maybe I'm missing something, but the only rules I have found so far are unclear. Can a Stalwart buy Mesmerist gifts, or vice versa? Can everyone buy gifts from the core rulebook and the player's guide, or is that restricted to Daredevils? A big shiny chart for experience costs and who can buy what (including the costs for increasing facets and paths) would be appreciated. Too much is buried in the text, or apparently just assumed. (The cost for a dot in a Path is particularly well hidden.) Just a quick explanation of which keywords were legal for each character type would help.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27869-bittergeek","name":"bittergeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27869_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T02:22:56-07:00","id":1520089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bittergeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1520085-what-gifts-can-each-type-of-character-buy#post1520085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I am unclear what types of gifts the characters can purchase with XP after character creation. Maybe I'm missing something, but the only rules I have found so far are unclear. Can a Stalwart buy Mesmerist gifts, or vice versa? Can everyone buy gifts from the core rulebook and the player's guide, or is that restricted to Daredevils? A big shiny chart for experience costs and who can buy what (including the costs for increasing facets and paths) would be appreciated. Too much is buried in the text, or apparently just assumed. (The cost for a dot in a Path is particularly well hidden.) Just a quick explanation of which keywords were legal for each character type would help.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>They can buy basically the gifts they can buy on character creation, what means:<br /> Stalwarts can buy Dynamic and Power gifts.<br /> Mesmerists can buy Psychic gifts.<br /> Daredevils can buy Lucky, Attributes and Skill gifts (but not Dynamic gifts), including the ones from Core.<br /> <br /> Notice that the Dynamic gifts dont have an specific tag, so you may need to pay attention on the source of the Gifts with Attribute tag.<br /> <br /> BUT, its perfectly possible to let Stalwarts to buy Attribute gifts fom Talents, most of them fits perfectly, other switches not so much...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-insp